          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}]</span></p><p>Substituting the above into the given expression, we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (\\sin^{2} x)/(\\sin 2x)|= (\\sin x\\sin x)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (\\sin x\\sin x)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (\\sin x)/(2\\cos x); = (1)/(2)\\tan x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n[MATH: \\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}]\n\nSubstituting the above into the given expression, we get\n\n[MATH: (\\sin^{2} x)/(\\sin 2x)|= (\\sin x\\sin x)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (\\sin x\\sin x)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (\\sin x)/(2\\cos x); = (1)/(2)\\tan x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
