          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, recall that \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}, \\qquad \\csc 2x = \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}\\sin 2x}.]</span></p><p>Now, using the double-angle formula for sine,\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x},]</span>\nwe simplify the expression as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\tan x\\csc 2x|= 2 \u22c5 (\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(\\sin 2x); = (2\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (2\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (1)/(\\cos^{2} x); = \\sec^{2} x]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, recall that\n[MATH: \\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}, \\qquad \\csc 2x = \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}\\sin 2x}.]\n\nNow, using the double-angle formula for sine,\n[MATH: \\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x},]\nwe simplify the expression as follows:\n\n[MATH: 2\\tan x\\csc 2x|= 2 \u22c5 (\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(\\sin 2x); = (2\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (2\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (1)/(\\cos^{2} x); = \\sec^{2} x]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nSimplify the expression [MATH: 2\\tan x \\csc 2x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, recall that\n[MATH: \\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}, \\qquad \\csc 2x = \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}\\sin 2x}.]\n\nNow, using the double-angle formula for sine,\n[MATH: \\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x},]\nwe simplify the expression as follows:\n\n[MATH: 2\\tan x\\csc 2x|= 2 \u22c5 (\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(\\sin 2x); = (2\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (2\\sin x)/(\\cos x) \u22c5 (1)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (1)/(\\cos^{2} x); = \\sec^{2} x]"
