        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWrite [MATH: \\cos{x}\\csc{x}\\sec^2{x}] as a single trigonometric function.\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we simplify the given expression using the following identities:\n\n[MATH: \\csc x = \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}, \\qquad\n\\sec x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}]\n\nSubstituting the above into our expression, we get\n\n[MATH: \\cos x\\csc x\\sec^{2} x|= \\cos x \u22c5 (1)/(\\sin x) \u22c5 (1)/(\\cos^{2} x); = (\\cos x)/(\\sin x\\cos^{2} x); = (\\cos x)/(\\sin x\\cos x\\cos x); = (\\cos x)/(\\sin x\\cos x\\cos x); = (1)/(\\sin x\\cos x).]\n\nNow, we recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n[MATH: 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}]\n\nSubstituting the above into our expression, we finally get\n\n[MATH: (1)/(\\sin x\\cos x)|= (2)/(2\\sin x\\cos x); = (2)/(\\sin 2x); = 2\\csc 2x.]"
